  "gaps": [
    "The capture contains complete requirement lists for two programs (Bachelor of Arts in Human Resources Management and Bachelor of Arts in Instructional Design); this ledger assumes the Human Resources Management program was intended. Confirm the target program.",
    "Global Campus Foundations is stated as 33 credits, and the program also states that 3 credits from the major (ECO 204, marked *) may satisfy Foundations requirements. The capture does not say which of the 11 standard Foundations courses ECO 204 replaces. As listed, the line items sum to 123 credits against a 120-credit total.",
    "The capture says Foundations courses 'may be substituted', but the substitution rules are not stated.",
    "GEN 101 (and GEN 104 for students transferring fewer than 30 credits) is scheduled and satisfies 3 elective credits each. The capture does not say whether these are mandatory components of the 45 elective credits.",
    "Residency requirement (minimum 30 credits completed at the University) is stated generally. No specific courses are designated as institution-only.",
    "Upper-division requirement: minimum 30 upper-division credits, including 18 upper-division credits in the major. The capture does not designate which electives must be upper-division.",
    "The program description mentions a required capstone, but the capture does not explicitly name the capstone course. MGT 490 'must be taken last in the program' and is listed as major rather than capstone.",
    "BUS 401 requires that the Quantitative Reasoning requirement be met first. The capture does not define which course satisfies Quantitative Reasoning.",
    "GPA requirement: minimum cumulative 2.00 in all coursework attempted at the University."
  ],
